You write what you know. When the bell rings, you set down your pen and breathe.

Midterm GPA: (print: $gpaMark)

[[Continue->January]]


:: Ending {"position":"650,400","size":"100,100"}
# The End of Senior Year
<img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1523240795612-9a054b0db644?auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80" alt="Graduation cap and diploma">

You did it. You made it through.

Whatever your result — whatever choices you made — this year asked something real of you. It asked you who you want to be when no one is watching.

The students who leaned on Cognito for everything did not just risk their grades. They robbed themselves of something harder to measure: the confidence that comes from knowing you did it. The knowledge that lives in your hands when you pick up a pen in a quiet exam room and realize — I actually know this.

Technology will keep changing. The tools will get smarter, faster, more convincing. But no algorithm can want something for you. No AI can care about your future.

That part was always yours.

[[Play Again->Start]]


:: Expelled {"position":"275,25","size":"100,100"}
# Expelled
<img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1693600411508-d7e9a9fef63a?auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80" alt="An empty school hallway">

The school administration has reviewed the evidence. The decision is final.

You are expelled from school.

Without a diploma, your university dreams are over — at least for now.

Integrity, once lost, is hard to rebuild. But it is never too late to start.

[[Play Again->Start]]


:: February {"position":"775,275","size":"100,100"}
(display: "StatDisplay")
# February — Surprise Test
<img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1484480974693-6ca0a78fb36b?auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80" alt="A checklist and pen">

You walk into first block and see it written on the board:

POP QUIZ — Please clear your desks.

You did not study for this. Nobody did.

[[Try your honest best->February Honest]]
[[Sneak a look at Cognito under the desk->February Cheat]]


:: February Cheat {"position":"1025,275","size":"100,100"}
(set: $usedAI to true)
(set: $ability to (max: 0, $ability - 4))
(display: "StatDisplay")
# Under the Desk

You get what looks like a solid answer from Cognito. You write it down.

Then — reading it back — you realize it is completely made up. Fabricated dates. Fake names. A hallucination.

You have already handed it in.

[[Tell the teacher before they grade it->February Confess]]
[[Say nothing and hope for the best->Expelled]]


:: February Confess {"position":"1150,275","size":"100,100"}
(set: $gpaTotal to $gpaTotal + 1.0)
(set: $gpaCount to $gpaCount + 1)
(set: $currentGPA to $gpaTotal / $gpaCount)
(set: $usedAI to false)
(display: "StatDisplay")
# Coming Clean

You go up after class, heart pounding.

"I made a mistake. I used AI and the answer was wrong. I am telling you now."

Your teacher looks at you for a long moment.

"I appreciate your honesty. This will still affect your grade — but I respect that you came forward."

GPA penalty applied | You remain enrolled

[[Continue->Late February]]


